fin-post-trade:DirectRightsDueBillCorporateActionProfile a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "The direct rights due-bill corporate action profile is an optional implementation profile that locks a corporate action event to the cash dividend, stock split, or non-transferable direct-rights issue kinds, with exactly one consideration per event and the due-bill entitlement transfer chain. It is the first concrete profile of the generic corporate action core and is not a universal corporate-action invariant; merger, redemption, conversion, tender, spin-off, exchange, transferable rights, interest, tax withholding, cash-in-lieu, and reversal/correction are admitted by the generic core under additional profiles and options.";
    rdfs:label "Direct Rights Due-Bill Corporate Action Profile";
