fin-post-trade:MissingSideAssertion a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "The missing side assertion is a probe-backed proof that, for one canonical comparison-key bucket, a specified side is absent from the case-selected complete internal projection set or the exact external statement-line set, while the opposite side is proven present by the finding's observable members. It is distinct from an IncompleteSourceCoverageAssertion, which states that a query returned no rows but coverage is unknown so absence cannot be concluded. Under the Strict Technical Settlement Reconciliation Profile the absence proof must be a deterministic side absence with a completed universe probe; the generic core admits weaker absence-proof kinds.";
    rdfs:label "Missing Side Assertion";
