fin-post-trade:ReconciliationFinding a owl:Class;
    rdfs:comment "The reconciliation finding is the exactly one deterministic matched, value-mismatch, duplicate, or missing-side result for a non-empty canonical comparison-key bucket, carrying all exact internal and external versions, used for characterizing the reconciliation conclusion for one comparison-key bucket. Under the Strict Technical Settlement Reconciliation Profile the finding is one-to-one per bucket; the generic core admits one-to-many, many-to-one, and many-to-many match groups via a ReconciliationMatchGroup, where duplicate means the same logical business fact recorded more than once rather than any bucket count greater than one.";
    rdfs:label "Reconciliation Finding";
